Build the Fastly CLI for GOOS=wasip1.

Reason: fastly v17.1.0 builds for wasip1 except for two modules.
github.com/mitchellh/go-ps (ps.Processes, which compute serve uses to find
a running Viceroy) has no wasip1 file, so processes and findProcess are
undefined. github.com/otiai10/copy (cp.Copy, which compute init uses for a
local --from directory) builds its named-pipe, lutimes and stat-times files
for every Unix but js, and wasip1 has no Mkfifo, Lutimes or Atim/Ctim. go-ps
gets a wasip1 file that answers "no process table"; otiai10/copy takes its
js/plan9 fallbacks on wasip1 (named pipes and symlink times are not copied,
times come from ModTime). compute serve and compute init are refused on
wasip1 before they reach either (0003).

Upstream: not filed (homescoop does not file upstream reports).
removeWhen: go-ps and otiai10/copy build for GOOS=wasip1 without it.

diff --git a/vendor/github.com/mitchellh/go-ps/process_wasip1.go b/vendor/github.com/mitchellh/go-ps/process_wasip1.go
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vendor/github.com/mitchellh/go-ps/process_wasip1.go
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+//go:build wasip1
+
+package ps
+
+import "errors"
+
+// errNoProcessTable is what wasip1 answers: slicc-kernel gives a WASI
+// program no process table to read.
+var errNoProcessTable = errors.New("go-ps: wasip1 has no process table")
+
+func findProcess(int) (Process, error) {
+	return nil, errNoProcessTable
+}
+
+func processes() ([]Process, error) {
+	return nil, errNoProcessTable
+}
